From a02c75b8616479f79f449919ac5d26e6f70b427a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonny Heggheim <hegjon@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 07:36:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] libalpm: install btrpkg packages from sync repositories

With BtrPkgHelper set (pacman.conf) and the cache directory on btrfs, a sync
target whose database entry has btrpkg.index and btrpkg.id in %DATA% is
downloaded as NAME.pkg.btr by the helper (btrpkg pull-ids: one download
queue per repository, data reused from the installed versions) instead of
%FILENAME%.

Validation: the index must parse and have the header ID from the database
(instead of %SHA256SUM%); with package signatures on, NAME.pkg.btr.sig must be
a signify signature by a key in /etc/btrpkg/keys or /usr/share/btrpkg/keys
(instead of the OpenPGP signature).

_alpm_open_archive reads a btrpkg cache file as a tar stream made from its
index (btrstream.c), so loading, file lists, .INSTALL, mtree and extraction
with backup files, .pacnew and NoExtract work unchanged. perform_extraction
reflinks large files from the cache file (FICLONERANGE, copy as fallback)
into a new file next to the target, sets owner, mode, xattrs and mtime, and
renames it into place; their data in the tar stream is skipped unread.

Without BtrPkgHelper nothing changes. test/btrpkg/btrtar lists an archive as
libalpm sees it: for 315 packages the stream from a btrpkg cache file matches
the original .pkg.tar.zst entry for entry, data included.
